       "before": "The parent driver of law X9 r1 item 3 and item 5's census (unit X9-0), under the test-only crash-matrix feature. MatrixChild re-executes the current test binary as current_exe() --exact <entry> --nocapture --test-threads=1 with a cleared environment holding only OPENSIP_X9_CHILD, OPENSIP_X9_INPUT, OPENSIP_X9_ARMS (absent for an untraced child) and TMPDIR, validates the arming before spawning, reads the child's stderr records on a reader thread and drains stdout, awaits a held or other event by blocking reads, writes addressed resumes on stdin, and kills with SIGKILL; dropping an unfinished child kills it. The per-run watchdog (300 s; shorter only in this crate's tests) is the one timed wait: it kills the child and the run can only be a HARNESS-ERROR. Exit verifies a finished child (exit 0, the entry ran, no harness-error, every arm reached) and item 3's death at a point (signal 9, the holding thread's last record is that held, and no later record names a durability point), and gives the outcome and the trace without the process id. Census takes a traced child with nothing armed into points with contiguous occurrences and durability, and derives the kill set: each durability point at #1 and, when repeated, at (n + 1) / 2 and n. Test-only; confers no authority.",
       "after": "The parent driver of law X9 r1 item 3 and item 5's census (unit X9-0), under the test-only crash-matrix feature. MatrixChild re-executes the current test binary as current_exe() --exact <entry> --nocapture --test-threads=1 with a cleared environment holding only OPENSIP_X9_CHILD, OPENSIP_X9_INPUT, OPENSIP_X9_ARMS (absent for an untraced child), OPENSIP_X9_CLOCK (law X9 r2 item 3, unit X9-1: <E>:<k> from the ChildSpec's ScriptedClock, the run set's epoch and the child's ordinal; absent without one, so the child reads the OS's wall clock) and TMPDIR, validates the arming and the clock script before spawning, reads the child's stderr records on a reader thread and drains stdout, awaits a held or other event by blocking reads, writes addressed resumes on stdin, and kills with SIGKILL; dropping an unfinished child kills it. The per-run watchdog (300 s; shorter only in this crate's tests) is the one timed wait: it kills the child and the run can only be a HARNESS-ERROR. Exit verifies a finished child (exit 0, the entry ran, no harness-error, every arm reached) and item 3's death at a point (signal 9, the holding thread's last record is that held, and no later record names a durability point), and gives the outcome and the trace without the process id. Census takes a traced child with nothing armed into points with contiguous occurrences and durability, and derives the kill set: each durability point at #1 and, when repeated, at (n + 1) / 2 and n. Test-only; confers no authority."
