       "after": "Produce the read side's premise receipt (law 458c r5 items 1 to 4): the process's one attempt, the actor, InitialCore and InitialPlatform, exactly the creator's producers, with no intent, storage choice, disclosure, effect or fence. Law X1 r1 items 1 and 2 type it by purpose: the one producer composition makes PlatformReceipt<Read> (ReadPremiseReceipt, produce_read_platform) or PlatformReceipt<Write> (WritePlatformReceipt, produce_write_platform); Read and Write are sealed, neither receipt converts into the other, and a receipt whose actor, core or platform belongs to another attempt is the invariant row. The read receipt is private and not Clone, holds its own attempt, and lends only the sealed ReadPremiseQualification that InitialPlatform alone implements: the check that a filesystem is H's and the omission premise with 465 item 4's scope, no barrier policy. The write receipt is likewise private, not Clone and holds its own attempt; its lending is the durable write gate's sealed DurableBarrierQualification, beside which it lends the running core's embedded bootstrap source to the fenced first read alone (law X4B r5 item 2, unit X4B-b), charge, one charged step on its attempt ledger with that lending (unit X2e), charge_guarded, the same step with the actor, core and platform rechecks lent beside it for the checkpoint's guard (law X4 r7 item 4, unit X4a), and the attempt ledger's one end-path settlement reserve and its single spend, on the commit session's way only (law X3d r6 item 8, unit X3d-1). Both purposes expose recheck, the actor, core and platform rechecks on the receipt's own attempt, and selected_core, the selected core's closure and state writer K as values only (law X3a item 1). Both also expose core_evaluator_closure, the selected core's evaluator closure (contract successor EC1) derived from the same authenticated inventory, as a value only (law X3d r8 item 13, unit X3d-3), and, only under the joint predicate (test, crash-matrix or scenario-fixtures), the read of its preimages behind CommitSession's test-support accessor. Every refusal ends in its law 468 item 6 row through 468c's maps. InstallationReadFence::acquire and doctor's installation check pass it to the observation session. The ordinary writer's admission consumes the write receipt (law X1), and the operation handoff carries it (unit X2e). Its one wired CLI path is opensip doctor (law X10), through doctor's installation check; no CLI command reaches a write receipt."
