or, which places its files where publish writes them (law X4B r5 item 9, unit X4B-c). bootstrapping_first_read is the body of the operation monitor's single first read at the lease-free point: X4T-b's fenced_first_read on the retained owner, then, only on F absent (TRUST.NO_ADMITTED_TIME_CONTEXT) and only for a fenced read that is not report-only, acceptance of the payload from BootstrapSource (the write receipt's running core, copied and charged only on that branch) on the read's own clock sample under the same fence hold, and the one confirming admission on the confirmed state.v1, whose view is returned. An acceptance refusal ends the read, and a second F absent is the host invariant row (TrustRow::Invariant); the order lives in first_read_sequence. It grants nothing: the confirming admission is X4T's own."
